From c92dcb6c4dad3ab1ec537e348f59928705923081 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Machado?= <machaddr@falanet.org>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:16:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: btrtl: preserve initialization errors before
 cleanup

A failed RTL_SEC_PROJ register read stores its error in rc, but the common
cleanup path returns ERR_PTR(ret). ret can still be zero after the earlier
successful ROM-version read. The initializer then returns NULL, which
passes its callers' IS_ERR checks and is dereferenced during firmware
download.

This matches the PineTab-V report: a register read fails with -EPROTO,
then btrtl_download_firmware+0xe faults loading ic_info through a NULL
btrtl_dev. Store the failing read's result in ret, the variable returned
by the common error path, and remove the redundant rc variable.

The drop-firmware command allocation failure has the same stale-zero
return problem. Set ret to -ENOMEM before cleaning up on that path too.
Callers now receive a real error pointer, so a controller initialization
failure returns its errno without causing a kernel Oops. This preserves
the error; it does not mask or solve the underlying USB protocol failure.

Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/bluetooth/btrtl.c?h=v7.3
Assisted-by: Codex (OpenAI)
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btrtl.c | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btrtl.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btrtl.c
index d298133..35a2c9d 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btrtl.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btrtl.c
@@ -1073,7 +1073,6 @@ struct btrtl_device_info *btrtl_initialize(struct hci_dev *hdev,
 	u16 hci_rev, lmp_subver;
 	u8 hci_ver, lmp_ver, chip_type = 0;
 	int ret;
-	int rc;
 	u8 key_id;
 	u8 reg_val[2];
 
@@ -1144,8 +1143,10 @@ next:
 
 	if (btrtl_dev->drop_fw) {
 		skb = bt_skb_alloc(sizeof(*cmd), GFP_KERNEL);
-		if (!skb)
+		if (!skb) {
+			ret = -ENOMEM;
 			goto err_free;
+		}
 
 		cmd = skb_put(skb, HCI_COMMAND_HDR_SIZE);
 		cmd->opcode = cpu_to_le16(0xfc66);
@@ -1185,8 +1186,8 @@ next:
 		goto err_free;
 	}
 
-	rc = btrtl_vendor_read_reg16(hdev, RTL_SEC_PROJ, reg_val);
-	if (rc < 0)
+	ret = btrtl_vendor_read_reg16(hdev, RTL_SEC_PROJ, reg_val);
+	if (ret < 0)
 		goto err_free;
 
 	key_id = reg_val[0];
-- 
